This week at the round
table of dim lighting,

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.910
we're asking the question, how was London?

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.580
- How was it?
- And then we're answering

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.210
that question 'cause as
of the recording of this,

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.590
we are still pretty fresh off of our trip

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.220
to London, England, United Kingdom,

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:30.853
Europe world.
- Not for long. (chuckles)

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.400
Yeah I still have jet lag.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.130
- I still am, well--
- Are you waking up?

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.870
I'm waking up like--
- It is eight hours ahead--

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.320
- Three o'clock.
- Of us.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.415
- I'm waking up like 3 a.m.
and I'm like ready to go

00:00:42.415 --> 00:00:44.400
and then I'm like don't,
you gotta go back to sleep.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.770
- Well the thing that I'm noticing is

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:51.330
at about seven o'clock at night--

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.260
- It hits you.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.260
- I get hit really hard
with this irritability that,

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:00.790
like I was out to dinner with the family

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.530
and they were all
talking about interacting

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:06.328
with one another, which I mean,

00:01:06.328 --> 00:01:08.100
if that's your thing.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.040
- Yeah, your family's talking.
- It was not my thing

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.400
at the time, I mean, I
stopped at one point,

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.040
I was like guys, I just wanna tell you,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.820
we're like halfway through the meal--

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.150
- I am so irritable right now.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:20.660
- I just feel like I could
explode with irritability

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.440
and I'm just like very testy.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:23.840
- You know, this is kinda crazy.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:27.010
'Cause you know how it's
manifested itself with me?

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:30.160
Extreme restless legs.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.780
- Really?
- Extreme restless legs.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.200
Now I have restless legs

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.703
(grunts) syndrome.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:38.100
(Link grunts)

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:42.360
I think I've talked about
this before, but anyway,

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:47.360
it's the irresistible urge to
move and what was happening is

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:52.260
it was in my right leg, it
started getting in my right hand.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.890
- Well hold on, this is only
when you're sleeping, right?

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:57.730
- No, it happens when,
it happens typically

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.900
when you're trying to go to sleep

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:02.760
but what was happening
which was so weird is that

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:07.760
because of the jet lag, it was
hitting me about 7:30 for me,

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.307
so on Monday night I was
in my therapy appointment,

00:02:12.307 --> 00:02:14.440
and I started having it real bad

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.710
and my leg was bouncing up and down

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:20.460
and I've never had it in my arm
and so my arm was also like,

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.480
I was moving around a lot.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.550
And my therapist was like,
you're very uncomfortable

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.237
with what we're talking
about right now, aren't you?

00:02:25.237 --> 00:02:27.410
And I was like, well, I mean yeah

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.980
but it's because I got
restless legs, brah.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:30.813
- In my arm.

00:02:30.813 --> 00:02:33.710
You got restless leg in your arm.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:36.270
Why not call it restless arm?

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:39.420
- I don't know what that
is and then the next night,

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:43.410
I went back to my therapist
with my wife, it's a long story.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.853
- Well let's go into it.

00:02:45.802 --> 00:02:46.940
(Link chuckles)

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.720
- We just needed an emergency session.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.900
- Okay.
- It was actually great.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:54.260
Incredible session, but
during that, it happened again

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:56.870
and I was, just thinking about it--

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.613
- Show me exactly what you were doing.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:03.957
- Like you see my foot?

00:03:03.957 --> 00:03:04.790
You see my foot?

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:06.150
My foot would be out like
this and I'd be like--

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:09.460
- Okay your foot's out, so
you're just waggling your foot.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.660
But what about your arm?

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.960
Okay you got a fist, you
got one hand in a fist

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.400
and you're grabbing it
with your other hand.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.540
- Just moving.
- You just look

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.040
very uncomfortable.
- Yeah I look like

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.700
I'm squirming my way out of something,

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.242
and maybe I was--
- Yeah like when you get sent

00:03:23.242 --> 00:03:25.880
to the principal's office
but you have to wait outside

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.660
and everyone's walking by going to lunch

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.101
and they see you sitting there.

00:03:29.101 --> 00:03:30.626
- Yeah.
- And you're like,

00:03:30.626 --> 00:03:34.200
his leg's twitching and he's
holding hands with himself.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.150
- Just to be clear 'cause
a lot of people think,

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.720
oh I tap my leg a lot, I must have,

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.370
that's not restless leg syndrome.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.860
So if you have a tendency
to let out excess energy

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.360
by bobbing your knee
up and down like that,

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.820
not restless legs, not the same thing.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.690
Restless legs is this,
you only can explain it

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:54.450
if you have it, it's
this irresistible urge

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:58.150
to move to the point that you
feel like you're going to,

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:01.400
it's so uncomfortable not to move.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.540
So it's not like the little thing

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:03.440
where you're just
bobbing up and down and--

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:04.860
- Well you know what--
- Don't wish it

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.690
on your worst enemy.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:07.940
- I'm sorry you have that, Rhett.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:10.170
- Okay, go ahead though.
- I don't have it.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.770
Never experienced it.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.713
I mean I'm only imagining
what it would be like

00:04:15.713 --> 00:04:17.720
just by hearing you describe it.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:20.700
- Right and I describe
it in such a vivid way.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.350
You don't even need to
watch the video version

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.010
of this podcast in order to get all the,

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:26.360
of course, maybe you
do because I did a lot,

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.950
a lot of physical things a second ago.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.247
Pretty impressive.

00:04:29.247 --> 00:04:30.856
- (chuckles) Well you shook your foot

00:04:30.856 --> 00:04:32.486
and that wasn't even in the shot.

00:04:32.486 --> 00:04:33.620
- (laughs) But you saw it.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.160
They can see your face looking at me.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.100
- Yeah, they can.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.370
Why are you yawning, man?

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:41.070
See, it's hitting you.
- I'm tired, man.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:43.003
- Jet lag, dude.
- I'm from London.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.190
I'm on London time.
- Once I told them I was about

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:50.430
to explode with irritability,

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:53.710
then it actually helped and
I didn't, for the record.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:56.270
- Yeah, separated yourself from it.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.370
You are not your emotions.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:01.730
- But, they seemed to not have heard me.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.010
It wasn't like they responded, it's like,

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.060
oh, thanks for sharing.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.200
They could have said that.
- Yeah.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.370
- They just kept talking,
but it made me feel good

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.780
to acknowledge that I had feelings instead

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.860
of letting those feelings control me.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.410
- Yeah.
- That's what I'm actually

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.180
trying to do and it was nice to know

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:21.153
that it was jet lag and
that I'm not just a jerk

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:24.050
that doesn't wanna be around
my family, because I do.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.900
- Yeah 'cause I thought
something was wrong with me,

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:29.190
it was so intense and
it was just the, no, no,

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:31.150
you would be asleep
right now and you're not.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:36.150
- Yeah because 7 p.m.
feels like, let's see,

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.030
plus eight--
- 3 a.m.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.403
- Is 15 a.m. which is 3 a.m.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.010
There's no 15 a.m.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.890
1500 hours would be 3 p.m.

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:47.238
- Right.
- There's no 15 a.m.

00:05:47.238 --> 00:05:48.320
- You just, the next day--
- You know,

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.460
we should change that.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:50.960
- They should just keep counting.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.440
They should count from
the beginning of time.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:53.960
- So we're going (chuckles)--

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:55.490
- That should be what time it is.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:59.220
- We've never been to London
so this podcast is gonna be us

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:03.160
sharing with you our first
ever experience in London

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.210
