00:10:32.647 --> 00:10:35.290
the stairs that lead up to my bedroom.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:37.763
So picture like a Harry
Potter kinda closet.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:41.320
You open the door to that closet,

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:42.232
there's a light switch in there.

00:10:42.232 --> 00:10:43.160
- Why didn't you just
put Britton in there?

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:45.080
- I thought about it.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.280
I did think about it, I was like hey,

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:48.310
if it's good enough for Harry--

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:50.581
- Yeah, give him something
to write a song about.

00:10:50.581 --> 00:10:53.164
(both chuckle)

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:55.410
- Have you been in this closet?

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:56.243
You open the door,

00:10:56.243 --> 00:10:58.330
you hit a light switch--
- I didn't know it was there.

00:10:58.330 --> 00:10:59.550
Next time I'm going in though.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:04.079
- When you open the
door, you're looking down

00:11:04.079 --> 00:11:08.690
the staircase that it goes,
if you look straight ahead

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:11.040
once you open the door,
it goes away from you

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:14.020
to, it slopes down to a point,

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:15.520
so you're not looking at it sideways

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:16.840
where it's sloping sideways.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:19.042
You're at the tallest point
and then it's sloping down

00:11:19.042 --> 00:11:20.603
to the floor.
- When you open the door.

00:11:20.603 --> 00:11:22.530
- When you open the door.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:25.810
And a matter of fact, it kinda slopes down

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:29.630
and then there's like a
cubby hole that I put,

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:31.900
stop yawning while I'm telling a story.

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.810
- It's boring, man. (chuckles)

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:36.410
- I know you're jet lagged
but it's not good for my ego.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:37.900
- Your story's boring. (chuckles)

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:39.690
- So it slopes down and it--
- You're talking about

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:42.060
the architecture of this
under the stairs room.

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:44.450
Is it important?
- The architecture's important

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:45.940
to what happened.
- Okay.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:47.850
- So you need to be
able to visualize this.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.670
You walk in, it's about six feet tall,

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:53.320
it immediately slopes down to
about two and a half feet tall

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:56.100
where there's a cubby hole
that I put the printer in.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:57.470
- Oh that's nice.
- Then in front

00:11:57.470 --> 00:12:00.300
of the printer, I put the safe.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:02.740
- In front of the printer.
- It's just a small safe.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.950
Four Trapper Keepers, then to the right,

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.300
there's enough room for a book shelf

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.700
that has all of our board
games that we used to keep

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.730
in Britton's room.
- Oh.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.260
Board games.
- So you can walk in

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:13.772
and get to the printer or
the safe or the board games.

00:12:13.772 --> 00:12:15.011
- You don't put the board
games in the safe, huh?

00:12:15.011 --> 00:12:17.480
- No, not enough room, I
don't have a walk-in safe.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:19.940
I could make this whole closet a safe.

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:22.185
- I got all my board
games in my walk-in safe.

00:12:22.185 --> 00:12:23.900
(chuckling)

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:26.030
- Chutes and Ladders is very flammable.

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:27.480
- Yeah, it's vintage edition.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:32.330
- It would be easy to get to
the printer and to the safe

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:33.930
except for the fact that
then at the last minute,

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:36.920
I realized I didn't know
where to put Jade's crate

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:40.623
so then I put it in right
smack dab in the middle.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:46.260
And it fills basically the
whole floor of the closet.

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:49.880
So when I go in there
to put the two passports

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:51.850
that are in my hand into the safe--

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:53.084
- You gotta move the crate.

00:12:53.084 --> 00:12:55.100
- But moving the crate is difficult

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:56.657
'cause it's almost the width of the door.

00:12:56.657 --> 00:12:59.250
- You gotta move the crate to print?

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:00.350
- Yeah.

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:01.916
Well--
- This is not sustainable.

00:13:01.916 --> 00:13:03.440
But--
- What you can do is

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:08.220
you can basically, I can
stand in front of the crate

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:13.220
and bend over, like hinge,
then put my hand on the crate

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:14.900
or somewhere and then kinda reach

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.290
and grab what I've printed.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:17.550
That's worked a few times.

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:19.100
- Easy.

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:22.513
- But the printer's a
foot higher than the safe.

00:13:22.513 --> 00:13:25.027
I didn't take into account this
was gonna be more difficult

00:13:25.027 --> 00:13:29.220
so I'm standing there, my
shin's against the front

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:33.239
of Jade's crate, then I hinge over

00:13:33.239 --> 00:13:37.920
and I realize, I can't reach
the safe so what I do is,

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.880
I take my hand and I extend
it out as far as I can

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.040
and when the slope goes down,

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:46.060
it then goes vertical for a two by four

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:49.350
and then goes horizontal
into the cubby hole

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:54.305
where the printer is, so there's
a little two by four height

00:13:54.305 --> 00:13:55.830
where--
- You rested your hand on.

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:57.650
- I rested my hand on that

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:01.800
and I'm pushing hard,
holding up my body weight

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:06.610
with my right hand and
then, I'm reaching down

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:10.033
with my left hand to open the safe.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:14.810
And I realize, well, I can't open the safe

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:16.490
with my left hand 'cause I've got--

00:14:16.490 --> 00:14:18.820
- My left hand doesn't know
the combination. (chuckles)

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:19.893
Only my right hand does.

00:14:19.893 --> 00:14:23.620
- Well there's no combination on my safe.

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:25.200
It's just for fire.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:26.850
It's not for theft.

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:29.550
All you gotta do is push, grab the handle,

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.363
push down on the safe.

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:33.620
- You don't have a combination?

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:36.950
- No, squeeze the handle,
and then it will open.

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:40.250
- My scans my eye before I walk in.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:41.113
- I don't care.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.470
- That's not true but you know.

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:45.723
- So then I'm like, I gotta switch hands

00:14:45.723 --> 00:14:47.830
so then I gotta get my
right hand down there

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:51.293
because the safe handle's
on the right side and so,

00:14:52.511 --> 00:14:55.530
I put my left hand up there
and I take my right hand down,

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:56.980
so now I'm--
- Always maintain

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.170
important contact.
- So now I am,

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:01.653
my whole upper body
weight is being held up

00:15:01.653 --> 00:15:04.231
with my left hand and then I reach down,

00:15:04.231 --> 00:15:07.353
again, I have the passports
in my hand but then

00:15:07.353 --> 00:15:11.550
with my other three fingers,
I'm gonna grab the handle,

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:15.770
push down on the safe,
pick it up all the way,

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:18.692
open the lid and then I'm
going to throw the things in

00:15:18.692 --> 00:15:20.406
and then I'm gonna close the lid

00:15:20.406 --> 00:15:22.930
and then I'm gonna unhinge myself

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:25.944
and I'm gonna get out of
there like a proud man.

00:15:25.944 --> 00:15:27.762
That's not how it happened.

00:15:27.762 --> 00:15:28.595
(Rhett sputters)

00:15:28.595 --> 00:15:31.080
So I'm holding myself up with my left hand

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:36.960
and I reach down to
grab the, open the safe,

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:40.490
and I open the safe and
as the lid is coming up

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:42.660
and I'm trying to pull the lid up,

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:45.850
my left hand slides--

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:47.950
- Yeah.
- Off of the two by four

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:50.010
that's holding my entire body weight up--

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.350
- Into the cubby.

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:54.000
- Yeah, and it goes into
air and then I just,

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:57.310
I start falling, so the
lid is up on the safe,

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:59.640
my hand is in a free-fall, my body begins

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:04.640
to be in a free-fall forward and the lid,

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:10.250
my right hand starts to fall
too and I try to catch myself

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:12.560
with my right hand 'cause
it's, I let go of the safe

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:14.480
and I turned my hand around to put my palm

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:16.690
toward the ground and catch myself,

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:21.690
but as I do that, the lid
of the safe comes down

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:24.380
on my fingertips--

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:26.900
- I think I see the finger
that got the brunt of it.

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:30.300
- And then the lid snaps
shut on my fingertips

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:33.386
while my left hand comes
down on top of the safe

00:16:33.386 --> 00:16:37.870
and pushes my entire body weight on top

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:42.870
of the safe lid, thereby
smooshing completely

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:45.200
my middle finger.

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:47.770
And I'm not just saying
the tip, I'm saying just,

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:52.020
it clamped down just below
the base of the finger.

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:53.850
- So basically the whole top part above

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:55.869
that knuckle was safe from fire.

00:16:55.869 --> 00:16:59.070
- Yes, it was, that is the
positive spin on this story.

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:03.372
The negative spin was that
I was in excruciating pain

00:17:03.372 --> 00:17:05.670
where I had--
- Say any wordy dirds?

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:09.190
- I had locked my middle finger--

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:10.710
- It locked?
- Of my right hand

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:15.250
into the safe and was
applying my full body weight

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:18.970
on top of it and I was
in like a yoga position

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:22.500
that you just can't magically hinge up.

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:25.590
You just can't magically,
like my feet are way back here

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:28.490
behind the kennel.
- The fire safe position.

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:30.210
- I was--
- Dad's doing fire safe.

00:17:30.210 --> 00:17:32.633
- I was like bent over a barrel basically.

00:17:33.550 --> 00:17:37.700
And I don't know, at that
point I'm like struggling

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.820
to get my finger out of the
safe and it won't come out.

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:40.700
I'm like (grunts).

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:42.160
I wasn't--
- Were you home alone?

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:45.120
- I was not saying English,
I was not saying expletives,

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:49.870
I was grunting like a
caveman in pain, agony,

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:54.166
and just total despair

00:17:54.166 --> 00:17:56.530
(chuckles) that I was
gonna be there forever.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:59.050
- But how soon after
that kinda thing happens,

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.240
like in the middle of
it, are you thinking,

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:02.860
I'm gonna talk about this on Ear Biscuits?

00:18:02.860 --> 00:18:05.290
(chuckles) Because--
- It hurt so bad.

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:07.120
- That's what happens to me now.

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:09.560
Anything that happens that is like,

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.340
I shouldn't have got
myself into this situation.

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:13.470
- Well I'll answer that because,

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:16.730
yeah what happened was, it
was an excruciating amount

00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:18.840
of pain and of course time
slows down at that point

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:23.840
but somehow, I was able
to hop my left hand

00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:28.550
off of the safe onto the floor
and then rip my right hand--

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:30.583
- Ugh.
- Out of the safe.

00:18:30.583 --> 00:18:31.416
- It was still closed though?

00:18:31.416 --> 00:18:33.310
- It didn't fully latch.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.010
That would have been impossible.

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:38.250
And then, I put both my
hands on the dog crate

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:40.713
and peeled myself back.

00:18:40.713 --> 00:18:42.350
- Well you could have
had trouble there too,

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:43.480
putting all your weight on the dog crate.

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:45.660
- Yeah and then--
- It'd collapse

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:47.170
the whole thing.

00:18:47.170 --> 00:18:49.450
- And then I don't know
if I immediately laid down

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:51.850
on the floor or did a
dance around the room,

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:56.570
but I looked at the
footage and you could hear,

00:18:56.570 --> 00:19:00.623
'cause I have that security
camera in that room.

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:05.267
But I was out of frame
but I played it back

00:19:05.267 --> 00:19:07.480
and I could hear the noise I made.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:08.547
It was like (grunting dramatically).

00:19:10.029 --> 00:19:12.862
(pained grunting)

00:19:16.939 --> 00:19:18.471
- [Christy] What's wrong?

00:19:18.471 --> 00:19:19.599
What's wrong?

00:19:19.599 --> 00:19:20.880
What did you do?

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:22.301
- [Link] My finger.

00:19:22.301 --> 00:19:27.301
I squeezed it into my finger. (laughing)

00:19:31.853 --> 00:19:33.275
(groans loudly)

00:19:33.275 --> 00:19:35.782
(tape fast forwards)

00:19:35.782 --> 00:19:38.124
(pained laughing)

00:19:38.124 --> 00:19:39.258
- [Christy] You're doing
something in there.

00:19:39.258 --> 00:19:41.555
What are you doing?

00:19:41.555 --> 00:19:43.113
- [Lando] Is it hurting?

00:19:43.113 --> 00:19:44.574
Are you hurting?

00:19:44.574 --> 00:19:46.520
- [Christy] He's hurting
and he's trying to laugh

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:47.818
at the pain away.

00:19:47.818 --> 00:19:48.701
(Rhett chuckles)

00:19:48.701 --> 00:19:51.550
- And then I was like
(groans dramatically).

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:52.512
- Did you save that?

00:19:52.512 --> 00:19:53.850
Did you save that clip?

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:55.033
- I got the clip, yeah.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:57.893
If it works we'll throw it in there.

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:02.390
And I'm like, while I'm laying
on the ground like (grunts),

00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:04.450
and like Christy comes
in there, she's like,

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:05.510
what's wrong?

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:06.780
She told me later she thought

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:08.282
that I'd fallen down the stairs.

00:20:08.282 --> 00:20:10.160
(Rhett laughs)

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:10.997
It's like the noises
you make when you are--

00:20:10.997 --> 00:20:12.497
- Your reaction--
- Falling down the stairs.

00:20:12.497 --> 00:20:14.510
- You must have fallen
down the stairs, no,

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:16.840
let me explain what I did,
it'll take 12 minutes.

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:18.830
- I would have been (chuckles), yeah,

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:22.330
I would have been falling
except I was laughing

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:24.550
and I was thinking about
how ridiculous this was

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:26.920
and that I was gonna share
it with you on Ear Biscuits

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:27.993
at that point.

00:20:29.216 --> 00:20:33.530
She got me some frozen peas
and she was like what happened?

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:36.680
And I was like, I smooshed
my finger in the safe.

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:38.030
I can't tell you the details

00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:39.900
because I feel kinda faint right now.

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:42.706
And I was thinking about what had happened

00:20:42.706 --> 00:20:47.050
and I started to feel
faint and I sat there

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:49.950
on my butt with frozen peas on my finger

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:51.820
for like 10 minutes
before I could feel like

00:20:51.820 --> 00:20:52.653
I could stand up.

00:20:52.653 --> 00:20:53.870
- You thought you might
have broken it maybe.

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.820
- Well I was convinced that
like I had lost my fingertip

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:58.800
or at least the nail.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:00.683
And I still may lose the nail.

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:02.630
Oh man it hurt.

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:04.857
It still hurts a little but but,

00:21:05.883 --> 00:21:09.580
oh man, I am so appreciative of nails.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:11.490
- You know what's kinda
interesting as well--

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:13.560
- If it wasn't for fingernails, yeah,

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:16.080
I would have lost the fingertip.

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.560
I think it's a protect, it's armor.

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:19.579
- I'm not gonna tell the story

00:21:19.579 --> 00:21:22.220
'cause it's not much of a
story but you know the finger

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:24.574
that I hurt before we left for London?

00:21:24.574 --> 00:21:26.580
I was telling you about
putting my hand into my

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:30.530
guitar case and the thing
going between my fingernail.

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:31.539
- Oh yeah.

00:21:31.539 --> 00:21:33.640
- It was the same
finger, the middle finger

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:36.040
of the right hand.
- The right hand.

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:36.873
- It's been swollen, see that?

00:21:36.873 --> 00:21:38.510
- You think this is a sign or something?

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:39.660
- It's been swollen ever since,

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:40.540
it's like I was worried that--

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:42.790
- You talking about the cutilage,

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:45.140
the cuticle on the right side of your--

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:46.580
- Yeah this thing went in and it bled.

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:48.360
It went down in there and then bled.

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:50.850
- I did that one time and it got infected.

00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:51.787
- That's what I thought was happening.

00:21:51.787 --> 00:21:56.425
- And it swelled up so big
that I super heated a needle

00:21:56.425 --> 00:22:00.690
underneath a flame and I stuck it in

00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:03.270
to drain all the puss out.

00:22:03.270 --> 00:22:06.180
- I thought I was gonna get
some sort of London bacteria.

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:08.998
You know like some old world bacteria

00:22:08.998 --> 00:22:10.793
that was gonna take me out.

00:22:11.840 --> 00:22:13.560
I don't know how bacteria works.

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:15.440
Okay, we're both fine though.

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:18.110
- Well I'm not fine, my
fingertip still hurts, brother.

