just love the way you funny.

01:03:03.070 --> 01:03:05.230
You know, I didn't say that.

01:03:05.230 --> 01:03:06.230
'Cause that doesn't even make sense

01:03:06.230 --> 01:03:08.540
but you know what I mean,
like that was my sense of,

01:03:08.540 --> 01:03:10.420
I really enjoy your humor.

01:03:10.420 --> 01:03:11.505
- It's the greatest.

01:03:11.505 --> 01:03:12.338
- It's the greatest.

01:03:12.338 --> 01:03:13.660
- It's the greatest, man.

01:03:13.660 --> 01:03:16.103
- It's the greatest humor,
it's so self-deprecating.

01:03:18.250 --> 01:03:20.350
And we made it back.

01:03:20.350 --> 01:03:23.490
Oh, did I meet J.J. Abrams on the plane?

01:03:23.490 --> 01:03:26.290
Perhaps. (chuckles dramatically)

01:03:26.290 --> 01:03:28.703
I mean I won't go into it but we're buds.

01:03:30.240 --> 01:03:31.510
Rhett was, you know...

01:03:33.540 --> 01:03:36.720
I pointed him out when we were waiting

01:03:36.720 --> 01:03:39.608
to get on the plane, we
were like sitting there.

01:03:39.608 --> 01:03:41.110
- Yeah.
- Pre-flight like

01:03:41.110 --> 01:03:41.943
sitting in the airport.

01:03:41.943 --> 01:03:43.900
- And then we start walking to our seats--

01:03:43.900 --> 01:03:44.733
- That's J.J. Abrams.

01:03:44.733 --> 01:03:49.170
He just finished filming
a Star Wars movie.

01:03:49.170 --> 01:03:50.850
- It's not just J.J. Abrams.

01:03:50.850 --> 01:03:55.040
I mean J.J. Abrams,
this guy is responsible

01:03:55.040 --> 01:03:59.210
for the revival of the Star Trek universe.

01:03:59.210 --> 01:04:01.073
- Star Wars.
- Star Wars.

01:04:02.205 --> 01:04:05.370
Shows that were on our list.

01:04:05.370 --> 01:04:07.660
- He's a brilliant--
- Of our most influential

01:04:07.660 --> 01:04:10.828
television, tale-ivision
shows, Alias and Lost.

01:04:10.828 --> 01:04:12.590
- What a brilliant entertainer.

01:04:12.590 --> 01:04:13.960
Writer, director, producer.

01:04:13.960 --> 01:04:15.740
Oh gosh, this dude.

01:04:15.740 --> 01:04:18.740
- And your seat was right next to him.

01:04:18.740 --> 01:04:19.890
- And I'm like (sighs).

01:04:22.200 --> 01:04:24.063
I made up my mind I
wasn't gonna talk to him.

01:04:24.910 --> 01:04:28.300
I respected him so much that
I didn't wanna do me to him.

01:04:28.300 --> 01:04:29.940
- But it was a 10 hour flight

01:04:29.940 --> 01:04:33.770
and you weren't exactly,
you were next to him but--

01:04:33.770 --> 01:04:36.930
- Did I look at what was on his phone

01:04:36.930 --> 01:04:38.420
throughout the entire flight, yeah.

01:04:38.420 --> 01:04:40.380
He played Words With Friends.

01:04:40.380 --> 01:04:42.660
He played some other
game I couldn't identify.

01:04:42.660 --> 01:04:44.023
He was texting people.

01:04:45.070 --> 01:04:46.440
Somebody was like, hey can you talk?

01:04:46.440 --> 01:04:48.020
And I was like why am I reading his texts?

01:04:48.020 --> 01:04:50.210
That's wrong and I didn't read the rest.

01:04:50.210 --> 01:04:53.390
But it was kinda in my
face, I wasn't like craning.

01:04:53.390 --> 01:04:56.163
Like he would hold up,
he was kinda leaned back,

01:04:56.163 --> 01:04:59.640
and he would hold his, I
don't know if he's nearsighted

01:04:59.640 --> 01:05:00.910
or something, he wasn't
wearing his glasses.

01:05:00.910 --> 01:05:04.580
He would hold his phone at
like full arms' length away.

01:05:05.780 --> 01:05:06.730
- So you could read his texts.

01:05:06.730 --> 01:05:08.880
- So that we could both read his phone.

01:05:08.880 --> 01:05:10.183
- It's like, Link.

01:05:11.601 --> 01:05:13.498
You seeing what I'm seeing here?

01:05:13.498 --> 01:05:14.648
(both chuckle)

01:05:14.648 --> 01:05:15.481
Yep.

01:05:15.481 --> 01:05:17.700
- He hadn't talked to me, and then--

01:05:17.700 --> 01:05:18.550
- You talked to him at the end.

01:05:18.550 --> 01:05:19.460
- Over the course of the flight,

01:05:19.460 --> 01:05:23.080
I was having this internal
dialogue about this dialogue.

01:05:23.080 --> 01:05:24.800
And also more importantly,

01:05:24.800 --> 01:05:26.950
the dialogue that I was
gonna have with my daughter.

01:05:26.950 --> 01:05:29.910
If I told Lily that I
sat next to J.J. Abrams

01:05:29.910 --> 01:05:32.570
and I did not speak to him,
she would be very angry.

01:05:32.570 --> 01:05:33.490
- Yeah.

01:05:33.490 --> 01:05:37.255
- Matter of fact, when I
got home and I was like,

01:05:37.255 --> 01:05:40.210
Lily, guess who I met?

01:05:40.210 --> 01:05:42.010
And we had a little yes or no game

01:05:42.010 --> 01:05:47.010
and she guessed J.J. and
she got tears in her eyes.

01:05:49.870 --> 01:05:54.223
Like literally, she was like so, like,

01:05:55.140 --> 01:05:59.500
just emotional about the fact
that I met him. (chuckles)

01:05:59.500 --> 01:06:02.370
So then I was validated
that I had made up my mind

01:06:02.370 --> 01:06:04.986
that when we're getting the
bags and he's about to walk out,

01:06:04.986 --> 01:06:07.930
and I noticed that a flight attendant,

01:06:07.930 --> 01:06:09.380
I'm not gonna call 'em a stewardess,

01:06:09.380 --> 01:06:11.740
came up to him like halfway
through the flight and was like,

01:06:11.740 --> 01:06:13.020
this was from another area of the plane

01:06:13.020 --> 01:06:15.650
and like crouched down and
talked to him for awhile

01:06:15.650 --> 01:06:17.800
and he was most gracious to her.

01:06:17.800 --> 01:06:20.183
- Oh super nice guy.
- And so I was like,

01:06:21.136 --> 01:06:26.136
I was like J.J., congratulations
on wrapping the shoot,

01:06:27.980 --> 01:06:31.630
and he looked at me like,
am I supposed to know you

01:06:31.630 --> 01:06:34.640
and I'm like, I just
saw the pictures online

01:06:36.123 --> 01:06:40.333
that were posted and he was
like, thanks man, thanks.

01:06:42.790 --> 01:06:46.030
And he was like, yeah I'm
really excited about it

01:06:46.030 --> 01:06:49.920
and I was like, well,
you're not the only one.

01:06:49.920 --> 01:06:52.950
He was like yeah yeah, I'm
just glad that this point,

01:06:52.950 --> 01:06:55.810
I was afraid at this
point, you're always afraid

01:06:55.810 --> 01:06:58.200
at this point meaning
when you're done shooting

01:06:58.200 --> 01:06:59.233
but haven't edited.

01:07:00.460 --> 01:07:02.110
You haven't gotten to that stage.

01:07:02.110 --> 01:07:03.590
You're not gonna have
everything, he's like,

01:07:03.590 --> 01:07:07.460
we got all of it, so he
gave me an assurance.

01:07:07.460 --> 01:07:09.420
- It's gonna be okay.
- He had everything he needed.

01:07:09.420 --> 01:07:11.970
- J.J. Abrams has got his--

01:07:11.970 --> 01:07:13.580
- He's got what--
- Stuff on lockdown.

01:07:13.580 --> 01:07:15.420
- He got what he needed.
- It's good to know.

01:07:15.420 --> 01:07:19.840
- And I was like you know
what, I'm sure you do, J.J.

01:07:19.840 --> 01:07:21.180
And that was pretty much it.

01:07:21.180 --> 01:07:23.140
I'm sorry I had to cut off
my conversation with you

01:07:23.140 --> 01:07:24.800
in order to turn and talk to him but,

01:07:24.800 --> 01:07:26.726
I was kinda in the middle
of our conversation,

01:07:26.726 --> 01:07:28.910
I just like whip pan--
- I understood.

01:07:28.910 --> 01:07:29.743
- Okay.

01:07:29.743 --> 01:07:32.040
- I was glad you initiated with him.

01:07:32.040 --> 01:07:34.430
I was glad you waited until
that moment to initiate

